  "id": "DrugBank_DB00547 - MONDO_grouped_4670_5282_19561",
  "verbalization": "Desoximetasone appears to be linked to Lupus Erythematosus through a chain of indications involving Prednicarbate and Flumethasone. The evidence suggests that Desoximetasone may act as a precursor or indirect agent in the treatment of Lupus Erythematosus, as it is associated with conditions like Granuloma Annulare and Discoid Lupus Erythematosus, which in turn are linked to Prednicarbate. Prednicarbate is a corticosteroid known to have immunosuppressive properties, and its association with Lupus Erythematosus implies a potential role in modulating immune responses. The presence of Flumethasone, a related compound, further suggests a possible pathway involving corticosteroids in the treatment of Lupus Erythematosus. The integrated evidence points to a mechanism where corticosteroids, through their immunosuppressive effects, may contribute to the management of Lupus Erythematosus, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
